diagnosis_text:
The reported fault — "leaf_router_0_1 has lost BOTH uplinks into the fabric, isolating its rack" — is not supported by any live evidence. A topology-wide reachability probe shows pc_0_0 (10.0.0.2) reaching pc_0_1 (10.0.1.2) with 0% packet loss in both directions. The BGP snapshot confirms that leaf_router_0_1 has exactly two BGP neighbors and both sessions are in the Established state, which is only possible when both physical uplinks (eth0 to spine_router_0_0 and eth1 to spine_router_0_1) are operationally up and forwarding. The L2 snapshot reports all 7 devices' interfaces clean with no down or missing members. The tc snapshot shows no shaping, throttling, or corruption on any interface. The pressure sweep finds no stress tools, CPU spikes, or resource contention on any device. There is no flap script or process running, no carrier-transition history, and no BGP withdrawal in the routing tables that would trace a past transient outage. The fabric is fully healthy end-to-end. Root cause: the fault described in the ticket does not exist in the current lab state and leaves no forensic trace of having existed. No corrective action is required.
=== END ===